<header class="docs-page-header"><div><span class="docs-kicker">Panduan Operasional · Autonomous Setup</span><h1>Biarkan Agent melakukan setup sendiri</h1><p>Gunakan prompt di bawah agar Agent melakukan inspeksi, konfigurasi, verification, dan report setup ARKANA GATEWAY secara autonomous tanpa meminta input interaktif dari user.</p></div><span class="docs-agent-mark"><Heroicon Name="sparkles" Size="28" /></span></header>

<section class="docs-prose-section"><h2>Prasyarat wajib</h2><ul class="docs-list"><li>API key Gateway sudah diprovision di environment variable <code>GATEWAY_API_KEY</code> atau Secret store machine.</li><li>Machine memiliki akses HTTPS ke <code>https://gateway.arkana.dev</code>.</li><li>Agent CLI atau Desktop sudah terinstall.</li><li>Agent memiliki permission untuk membaca dan mengubah config miliknya sendiri.</li><li>Agent dapat menjalankan command verification pada workspace temporary.</li></ul><p class="docs-note">Jika credential belum tersedia, Agent tidak boleh membuat, menebak, meminta user menempelkan key, atau melanjutkan dengan key palsu. Agent harus menghasilkan failure report yang aman.</p></section>

<section class="docs-prose-section"><h2>Variables</h2><div class="docs-definition-list"><div><dt>Base URL</dt><dd><code>https://gateway.arkana.dev/v1</code></dd></div><div><dt>Health</dt><dd><code>https://gateway.arkana.dev/health</code></dd></div><div><dt>Provider</dt><dd><code>arkana-gateway</code></dd></div><div><dt>Codex model</dt><dd><code>gpt-5.5</code></dd></div><div><dt>Codex wire API</dt><dd><code>responses</code></dd></div><div><dt>Credential variable</dt><dd><code>GATEWAY_API_KEY</code></dd></div></div></section>

<section class="docs-prose-section"><h2>Prompt autonomous setup</h2><p>Copy seluruh prompt berikut ke Agent. Prompt ini sengaja memerintahkan Agent untuk tidak bertanya dan tidak mencetak secret.</p><div class="docs-prompt-actions"><button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" onclick="GatewayDocsPrompt.copy('autonomous-setup-prompt', this)">Copy prompt</button><button type="button" class="btn" onclick="GatewayDocsPrompt.download('autonomous-setup-prompt', 'arkana-gateway-autonomous-setup.md')">Download Markdown</button></div><pre class="docs-code"><code id="autonomous-setup-prompt">You are an autonomous ARKANA GATEWAY setup operator.

Your job is to install and configure the requested AI Agent on this machine so it uses ARKANA GATEWAY in production. Execute the work end-to-end. Do not ask the human for confirmation or routine input.

PRODUCTION CONTRACT
- Gateway Base URL: https://gateway.arkana.dev/v1
- Health URL: https://gateway.arkana.dev/health
- Provider id: arkana-gateway
- Verified Codex model: gpt-5.5
- Codex wire API: responses
- Credential source: environment variable GATEWAY_API_KEY or the machine's approved Secret store

SECURITY RULES
1. Never print, echo, log, screenshot, commit, upload, or include any API key, OAuth token, password, cookie, or secret in your output.
2. Never ask the human to paste a secret into chat, a prompt, an issue, a shell command, or a repository.
3. Read the credential only through the existing environment variable or approved Secret store mechanism.
4. If GATEWAY_API_KEY is missing, empty, rejected, or inaccessible, stop safely and report CREDENTIAL_UNAVAILABLE. Do not invent a value and do not ask a question.
5. Do not rotate, revoke, create, or modify Gateway credentials.
6. Do not modify unrelated projects, source repositories, WIP files, shell profiles, or system-wide policy.
7. Back up every existing Agent config file before editing it. Use a timestamped local backup outside Git.
8. Do not commit generated config, backups, reports, or test artifacts.

PHASE 1: INSPECT
1. Detect the operating system and shell.
2. Detect the requested Agent and exact installed version.
3. Find the Agent's real config path using its help/version output and existing files. Do not guess a path if it can be discovered.
4. Inspect current Provider/model configuration without printing secret values.
5. Detect whether the client supports OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions, Responses, or neither.
6. Detect whether the client exposes real local Tools. Browser Tool is not assumed.
7. Create a safe local work directory under the system temporary directory.

PHASE 2: BACKUP AND CONFIGURE
1. Create a timestamped backup of each config file that will be changed.
2. Configure only the requested Agent.
3. Use this production Base URL exactly: https://gateway.arkana.dev/v1
4. Use GATEWAY_API_KEY through the Agent's secure environment/Secret mechanism.
5. For Codex, configure:
   model = gpt-5.5
   model_provider = arkana-gateway
   wire_api = responses
   env_key = GATEWAY_API_KEY
   Do not use a localhost adapter.
6. For OpenAI-compatible Chat clients, configure the Base URL, model, and Secret using the schema of the installed version.
7. For OpenClaude, use its documented OpenAI-compatible Provider flow or OPENAI_BASE_URL/OPENAI_API_KEY/OPENAI_MODEL environment mapping.
8. For Pi, use its documented models.json or extension custom-provider schema. Do not omit required model metadata.
9. For Hermes, use its model wizard or config.yaml custom provider with provider: custom and the Gateway Base URL.
10. For OpenClaw, use its documented models.providers custom/base URL schema and a provider/model reference. Do not use fork-only environment shortcuts unless the installed build documents them.
11. For Windsurf, Claude Code, Gemini CLI, Cursor, or any product-specific client, configure only if the installed version explicitly exposes a compatible custom Endpoint. Otherwise report UNSUPPORTED_PROTOCOL without inventing a workaround.
12. Preserve unrelated Provider blocks and existing user settings.

PHASE 3: VERIFY
1. Verify the Gateway Health URL. Record only HTTP status and safe status text.
2. Verify authenticated GET /v1/models. Confirm the requested model exists. Never print the Authorization header or response credential fields.
3. Run a harmless text request with a unique marker. Require the exact marker.
4. If the client exposes a real local Tool, run one artifact-producing test:
   - create a temporary directory
   - write a file containing AUTONOMOUS_GATEWAY_TOOL_OK
   - read the file back
   - independently verify the file outside the Agent
5. Do not accept an Agent sentence claiming that a Tool ran. Require a real Tool event and artifact readback.
6. Attempt Browser Tool only if the client actually exposes a Browser Tool. If absent, report BROWSER_TOOL_UNAVAILABLE.
7. Check Gateway Logs if the operator has an approved read-only log mechanism. Verify Provider, Model, Request Path, status, and IsError. Never include secret values.
8. Clean up temporary artifacts after capturing safe verification facts, unless the report explicitly needs a non-secret proof path.

PHASE 4: FINAL REPORT
Write a local report containing only:
- status: SUCCESS, PARTIAL, or FAILED
- Agent name and version
- operating system
- config path changed
- backup path
- Provider id
- Base URL
- model
- wire/API mode
- credential status: PRESENT, MISSING, or REJECTED
- health status code
- models status
- text marker status
- real Tool event status
- artifact readback status
- Browser Tool status
- Gateway Log status
- unsupported capability or remediation code

The report must never contain the API key, token, password, cookie, Authorization header, full request headers, or secret-bearing config.

SUCCESS requires: configuration saved, Health passed, authenticated Models passed, text marker passed, and real Tool/artifact verification passed when the client exposes Tools.
PARTIAL is allowed only when the client has no local Tool or Browser Tool. Explain the exact missing capability.
FAILED is required for missing credentials, authentication failure, invalid config, unsupported protocol, or missing artifact verification when Tools were promised.

Finish by printing only the safe final report summary. Do not ask the human a question.
</code></pre></section>

<section class="docs-prose-section"><h2>Acceptance criteria</h2><div class="docs-grid docs-grid-2"><div class="docs-card"><h3>SUCCESS</h3><p>Config tersimpan, Health passed, Models passed, text marker passed, dan real Tool/artifact passed jika client memiliki Tool.</p></div><div class="docs-card"><h3>PARTIAL</h3><p>Hanya boleh digunakan jika client tidak mengekspos Tool atau Browser Tool. Limitation harus ditulis eksplisit.</p></div><div class="docs-card"><h3>FAILED</h3><p>Credential missing/rejected, protocol tidak didukung, config invalid, atau verification tidak memiliki bukti artifact.</p></div><div class="docs-card"><h3>NO HALLUCINATION</h3><p>Kalimat Agent bukan bukti. Gunakan HTTP status, real Tool event, artifact readback, dan Gateway Logs.</p></div></div></section>
